# Template of rollup.conf for rollup.sh (TD-444 step 5 runbook §5.1). Installed root-only
# next to the script. Sources and paths are the design paths of the runbook (§2); the
# snapshot root is the btrfs subvolume (shared folder) the source lives in.
# Prune stays off until the source passed its restore drill (§5.1 per-source switch).
# F1/F2 are added only after the Finance owner confirmed their format (runbook §0, 2b),
# together with their absent() alerts.
# registry-data needs registry-data.digests next to this file: the digests that must stay
# restorable, one <repository>@sha256:<hex> per line (runbook §3.8 item 1).
# minio is read back through a throwaway MinIO (minio-readback.sh, runbook §3.8 item 2). It
# needs docker and these two settings; replace both placeholders, the roll-up refuses them:
#   MINIO_IMAGE        the live MinIO's image, pinned: sha256:<image id>, as printed by
#                      `docker inspect -f '{{.Image}}' <live MinIO container>`, or <repo>@sha256:<digest>
#   MINIO_CREDENTIALS  a root-only file (chmod 600) with MINIO_ROOT_USER=... and
#                      MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=... lines, no quotes; it never goes into git or a log
MINIO_IMAGE=sha256:<image-id-of-the-live-minio>
MINIO_CREDENTIALS=<root-only-credentials-file>
#
# name                   kind           source dir                                      snapshot root         prune
minio                    minio          /volume2/minio-backup/data                      /volume2/minio-backup off
registry-data            registry       /volume2/k3s-fast/cicd-registry-data            /volume2/k3s-fast     off
logical-backup-hot       logical        /volume2/k3s-fast/data-logical-backup-hot       /volume2/k3s-fast     off
gitea-backup             gitea          /volume2/k3s-fast/cicd-gitea-backup             /volume2/k3s-fast     off
cluster-state-backup     cluster-state  /volume2/k3s-fast/kube-system-cluster-state-backup  /volume2/k3s-fast off
